the target language is: lps.

% world.le — the interactive-fiction library, phase 1 of docs/InformPlan.md.
%
% A sliver of Inform's Standard Rules, written as Logical English for LPS: the
% physical world (rooms, things, containers, supporters, doors, people, the
% map), a dozen actions with their preconditions and effects, scenes, the
% clock, and one goal-seeking plan. A story includes it:
%
%     the knowledge base my story includes these resources: world.
%
% and adds its rooms, things, initial state and its own rules.
%
% Three conventions carried over from phase 0 (examples/if/phase0/):
%
%   * A command is not an obligation. Every command becomes `player tries to
%     …`, a composite event whose first clause is the action and whose second
%     is a refusal. The constraint refuses the first clause and the engine
%     backtracks into the second. `why_not(happened(Action), T)` then names the
%     constraint and the fluent behind it — which is the refusal message.
%   * Story time is a fluent. The driver injects `the turn begins` with each
%     command and `the turn ends` when the cycle has settled; `the turn is N`
%     counts turns, and anything scheduled names a turn.
%   * Text is not here. What happened is the trace; what it says is narration,
%     an edge concern (phase 2).
%
% Logical English wants one condition per line, `and` first. That is not a
% style choice: a conjunction written on one line is read as one sentence.

the events are:
    the turn begins; known as begin_turn.
    the turn ends; known as end_turn.
    the command is to look; known as cmd_look.
    the command is to examine *a thing*; known as cmd_examine.
    the command is to take inventory; known as cmd_inventory.
    the command is to wait; known as cmd_wait.
    the command is to take *a thing*; known as cmd_take.
    the command is to drop *a thing*; known as cmd_drop.
    the command is to put *a thing* into *a container*; known as cmd_insert.
    the command is to put *a thing* onto *a supporter*; known as cmd_put_on.
    the command is to open *a thing*; known as cmd_open.
    the command is to close *a thing*; known as cmd_close.
    the command is to lock *a thing* with *a key*; known as cmd_lock.
    the command is to unlock *a thing* with *a key*; known as cmd_unlock.
    the command is to go *a direction*; known as cmd_go.
    the command is to enter *a thing*; known as cmd_enter.
    the command is to exit; known as cmd_exit.
    *a person* tries to take *a thing*; known as try_take.
    *a person* tries to drop *a thing*; known as try_drop.
    *a person* tries to put *a thing* into *a container*; known as try_insert.
    *a person* tries to put *a thing* onto *a supporter*; known as try_put_on.
    *a person* tries to open *a thing*; known as try_open.
    *a person* tries to close *a thing*; known as try_close.
    *a person* tries to lock *a thing* with *a key*; known as try_lock.
    *a person* tries to unlock *a thing* with *a key*; known as try_unlock.
    *a person* tries to go *a direction*; known as try_go.
    *a person* tries to enter *a thing*; known as try_enter.
    *a person* tries to exit; known as try_exit.
    *a person* fetches *a thing*; known as fetch.
    *a person* opens up *a thing*; known as open_up.

the actions are:
    *a person* looks; known as look.
    *a person* examines *a thing*; known as examine.
    *a person* takes inventory; known as inventory.
    *a person* waits; known as wait.
    *a person* takes *a thing*; known as take.
    *a person* drops *a thing*; known as drop.
    *a person* puts *a thing* into *a container*; known as insert.
    *a person* puts *a thing* onto *a supporter*; known as put_on.
    *a person* opens *a thing*; known as open.
    *a person* closes *a thing*; known as shut.
    *a person* locks *a thing* with *a key*; known as lock.
    *a person* unlocks *a thing* with *a key*; known as unlock.
    *a person* goes *a direction*; known as go.
    *a person* enters *a thing*; known as enter.
    *a person* exits; known as exit.
    *a person* cannot take *a thing*; known as refuse_take.
    *a person* cannot drop *a thing*; known as refuse_drop.
    *a person* cannot put *a thing* into *a container*; known as refuse_insert.
    *a person* cannot put *a thing* onto *a supporter*; known as refuse_put_on.
    *a person* cannot open *a thing*; known as refuse_open.
    *a person* cannot close *a thing*; known as refuse_close.
    *a person* cannot lock *a thing* with *a key*; known as refuse_lock.
    *a person* cannot unlock *a thing* with *a key*; known as refuse_unlock.
    *a person* cannot go *a direction*; known as refuse_go.
    *a person* cannot enter *a thing*; known as refuse_enter.
    *a person* cannot exit; known as refuse_exit.

the fluents are:
    the turn is *a number*; known as turn.
    *a thing* is in *a holder*; known as in.
    *a thing* is on *a supporter*; known as on.
    *a person* carries *a thing*; known as carries.
    *a person* wears *a thing*; known as wears.
    *a thing* is closed; known as closed.
    *a thing* is locked; known as locked.
    *a scene* is playing; known as playing.
    *a scene* has ended *a way*; known as ended.
    the location of *a thing* is *a room*; known as location.
    *a thing* is accessible; known as accessible.
    *a person* can reach *a thing*; known as reachable.
    *a direction* from *a room* leads to *a second room*; known as leads.

the templates are:
    *a thing* is a room.
    *a thing* is a container.
    *a thing* is a supporter.
    *a thing* is a door.
    *a thing* is a person.
    *a thing* is openable.
    *a thing* is lockable.
    *a thing* is enterable.
    *a thing* is fixed in place.
    the key of *a thing* is *a key*.
    *a direction* from *a room* goes to *a second room*.
    *a direction* is opposite to *a second direction*.
    *a door* leads *a direction* from *a room* to *a second room*.

the knowledge base world includes:

% ---- the player and the compass

player is a person.

north is opposite to south.
south is opposite to north.
east is opposite to west.
west is opposite to east.
up is opposite to down.
down is opposite to up.
northeast is opposite to southwest.
southwest is opposite to northeast.
northwest is opposite to southeast.
southeast is opposite to northwest.

% ---- the clock

when the turn begins
then the turn that is a number becomes number + 1.

% ---- the map: a stated connection runs both ways unless the story says
%      otherwise, and a door is a connection that is shut when it is closed

a direction from a room leads to a second room at a time if
    the direction from the room goes to the second room.

a direction from a room leads to a second room at a time if
    a second direction from the second room goes to the room
    and the second direction is opposite to the direction.

a direction from a room leads to a second room at a time if
    a door leads the direction from the room to the second room
    and it is not the case that the door is closed at the time.

a direction from a room leads to a second room at a time if
    a door leads a second direction from the second room to the room
    and the second direction is opposite to the direction
    and it is not the case that the door is closed at the time.

% ---- where things are: the room that ultimately holds a thing

the location of a thing is a room at a time if
    the thing is in the room at the time
    and the room is a room.

the location of a thing is a room at a time if
    the thing is in a holder at the time
    and it is not the case that the holder is a room
    and the location of the holder is the room at the time.

the location of a thing is a room at a time if
    the thing is on a supporter at the time
    and the location of the supporter is the room at the time.

the location of a thing is a room at a time if
    a person carries the thing at the time
    and the location of the person is the room at the time.

the location of a thing is a room at a time if
    a person wears the thing at the time
    and the location of the person is the room at the time.

% ---- what can be got at: nothing shut inside a closed container

a thing is accessible at a time if
    the thing is in a room at the time
    and the room is a room.

a thing is accessible at a time if
    the thing is in a container at the time
    and it is not the case that the container is a room
    and it is not the case that the container is closed at the time
    and the container is accessible at the time.

a thing is accessible at a time if
    the thing is on a supporter at the time
    and the supporter is accessible at the time.

a thing is accessible at a time if
    a person carries the thing at the time.

a thing is accessible at a time if
    a person wears the thing at the time.

a person can reach a thing at a time if
    the person carries the thing at the time.

a person can reach a thing at a time if
    the person wears the thing at the time.

a person can reach a thing at a time if
    the location of the person is a room at the time
    and the location of the thing is the room at the time
    and the thing is accessible at the time.

% ---- causal laws: Inform's carry-out rules

when a person takes a thing
then the person carries the thing.

when a person takes a thing
then it is not the case that the thing is in a holder.

when a person takes a thing
then it is not the case that the thing is on a supporter.

when a person drops a thing
    and the person is in a holder
then the thing is in the holder.

when a person drops a thing
    and the person is on a supporter
then the thing is on the supporter.

when a person drops a thing
then it is not the case that the person carries the thing.

when a person puts a thing into a container
then the thing is in the container.

when a person puts a thing into a container
then it is not the case that the person carries the thing.

when a person puts a thing onto a supporter
then the thing is on the supporter.

when a person puts a thing onto a supporter
then it is not the case that the person carries the thing.

when a person opens a thing
then it is not the case that the thing is closed.

when a person closes a thing
then the thing is closed.

when a person locks a thing with a key
then the thing is locked.

when a person unlocks a thing with a key
then it is not the case that the thing is locked.

when a person goes a direction
    and the person is in a room
    and the direction from the room leads to a second room
then the person is in the second room.

when a person goes a direction
    and the person is in a room
then it is not the case that the person is in the room.

when a person enters a thing
    and the thing is a container
then the person is in the thing.

when a person enters a thing
    and the thing is a supporter
then the person is on the thing.

when a person enters a thing
    and the person is in a holder
then it is not the case that the person is in the holder.

when a person enters a thing
    and the person is on a supporter
then it is not the case that the person is on the supporter.

when a person exits
    and the person is in a holder
    and the holder is in a place
then the person is in the place.

when a person exits
    and the person is on a supporter
    and the supporter is in a place
then the person is in the place.

when a person exits
    and the person is in a holder
then it is not the case that the person is in the holder.

when a person exits
    and the person is on a supporter
then it is not the case that the person is on the supporter.

% ---- preconditions: Inform's check rules, without their messages.
%      A refusal is explained by why_not, which names the sentence.

it must not be true that
    a person takes a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person can reach the thing at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person takes a thing from a first time to a second time
    and the person carries the thing at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person takes a thing from a first time to a second time
    and the thing is fixed in place.

it must not be true that
    a person takes a thing from a first time to a second time
    and the thing is a person.

it must not be true that
    a person takes a thing from a first time to a second time
    and a second person carries the thing at the first time
    and the second person is different from the person.

it must not be true that
    a person takes a thing from a first time to a second time
    and the person is in the thing at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person drops a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person carries the thing at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person puts a thing into a container from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person carries the thing at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person puts a thing into a container from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the container is a container.

it must not be true that
    a person puts a thing into a container from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person can reach the container at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person puts a thing into a container from a first time to a second time
    and the container is closed at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person puts a thing into a container from a first time to a second time
    and the thing is equal to the container.

it must not be true that
    a person puts a thing onto a supporter from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person carries the thing at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person puts a thing onto a supporter from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the supporter is a supporter.

it must not be true that
    a person puts a thing onto a supporter from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person can reach the supporter at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person opens a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the thing is openable.

it must not be true that
    a person opens a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the thing is closed at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person opens a thing from a first time to a second time
    and the thing is locked at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person opens a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person can reach the thing at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person closes a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the thing is openable.

it must not be true that
    a person closes a thing from a first time to a second time
    and the thing is closed at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person closes a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person can reach the thing at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person locks a thing with a key from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the thing is lockable.

it must not be true that
    a person locks a thing with a key from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the thing is closed at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person locks a thing with a key from a first time to a second time
    and the thing is locked at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person locks a thing with a key from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the key of the thing is the key.

it must not be true that
    a person locks a thing with a key from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person carries the key at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person locks a thing with a key from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person can reach the thing at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person unlocks a thing with a key from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the thing is locked at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person unlocks a thing with a key from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the key of the thing is the key.

it must not be true that
    a person unlocks a thing with a key from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person carries the key at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person unlocks a thing with a key from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person can reach the thing at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person goes a direction from a first time to a second time
    and the person is in a holder at the first time
    and it is not the case that the holder is a room.

it must not be true that
    a person goes a direction from a first time to a second time
    and the person is on a supporter at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person goes a direction from a first time to a second time
    and the person is in a room at the first time
    and the room is a room
    and it is not the case that the direction from the room leads to a second room at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person enters a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the thing is enterable.

it must not be true that
    a person enters a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person can reach the thing at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person enters a thing from a first time to a second time
    and the thing is closed at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person enters a thing from a first time to a second time
    and the person is in the thing at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person enters a thing from a first time to a second time
    and the person is on the thing at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person exits from a first time to a second time
    and the person is in a room at the first time
    and the room is a room.

it must not be true that
    a person exits from a first time to a second time
    and the person is in a container at the first time
    and the container is closed at the first time.

% ---- the player's commands. A command is a try, never an obligation.

if the command is to look from a first time to a second time
then player looks from the second time to a third time.

if the command is to examine a thing from a first time to a second time
then player examines the thing from the second time to a third time.

if the command is to take inventory from a first time to a second time
then player takes inventory from the second time to a third time.

if the command is to wait from a first time to a second time
then player waits from the second time to a third time.

if the command is to take a thing from a first time to a second time
then player tries to take the thing from the second time to a third time.

if the command is to drop a thing from a first time to a second time
then player tries to drop the thing from the second time to a third time.

if the command is to put a thing into a container from a first time to a second time
then player tries to put the thing into the container from the second time to a third time.

if the command is to put a thing onto a supporter from a first time to a second time
then player tries to put the thing onto the supporter from the second time to a third time.

if the command is to open a thing from a first time to a second time
then player tries to open the thing from the second time to a third time.

if the command is to close a thing from a first time to a second time
then player tries to close the thing from the second time to a third time.

if the command is to lock a thing with a key from a first time to a second time
then player tries to lock the thing with the key from the second time to a third time.

if the command is to unlock a thing with a key from a first time to a second time
then player tries to unlock the thing with the key from the second time to a third time.

if the command is to go a direction from a first time to a second time
then player tries to go the direction from the second time to a third time.

if the command is to enter a thing from a first time to a second time
then player tries to enter the thing from the second time to a third time.

if the command is to exit from a first time to a second time
then player tries to exit from the second time to a third time.

% ---- trying: the action, or else the refusal

a person tries to take a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person takes the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to take a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person cannot take the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to drop a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person drops the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to drop a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person cannot drop the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to put a thing into a container from a first time to a second time if
    the person puts the thing into the container from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to put a thing into a container from a first time to a second time if
    the person cannot put the thing into the container from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to put a thing onto a supporter from a first time to a second time if
    the person puts the thing onto the supporter from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to put a thing onto a supporter from a first time to a second time if
    the person cannot put the thing onto the supporter from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to open a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person opens the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to open a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person cannot open the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to close a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person closes the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to close a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person cannot close the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to lock a thing with a key from a first time to a second time if
    the person locks the thing with the key from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to lock a thing with a key from a first time to a second time if
    the person cannot lock the thing with the key from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to unlock a thing with a key from a first time to a second time if
    the person unlocks the thing with the key from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to unlock a thing with a key from a first time to a second time if
    the person cannot unlock the thing with the key from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to go a direction from a first time to a second time if
    the person goes the direction from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to go a direction from a first time to a second time if
    the person cannot go the direction from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to enter a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person enters the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to enter a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person cannot enter the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to exit from a first time to a second time if
    the person exits from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to exit from a first time to a second time if
    the person cannot exit from the first time to the second time.

% ---- fetching: Inform's "Before someone taking something in a closed
%      container" and "Before someone opening a locked thing", as one plan.
%      A character asked to fetch something opens what is in the way, and
%      unlocks what is locked if it carries the key. The engine finds the
%      steps; the story only asks.

a person fetches a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person can reach the thing at the first time
    and the person takes the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person fetches a thing from a first time to a third time if
    the thing is in a container at the first time
    and the container is closed at the first time
    and the person opens up the container from the first time to a second time
    and the person takes the thing from the second time to the third time.

a person opens up a thing from a first time to a second time if
    it is not the case that the thing is locked at the first time
    and the person opens the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person opens up a thing from a first time to a third time if
    the thing is locked at the first time
    and the key of the thing is a key
    and the person carries the key at the first time
    and the person unlocks the thing with the key from the first time to a second time
    and the person opens the thing from the second time to the third time.
